id: brace
name: Brace
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
exploitable: All adjacent Opponents.
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Set yourself against the weather. Until the start of your next turn, Battle Weathers
  count a Tier lower - two Tiers with 4+ Ranks in Survival, and a Tier of 0 is a
  Weather that does nothing to you.
text: >
  Brace Maneuver [1/Round]: Prepare yourself to withstand the weather.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: Free
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: All adjacent Opponents.
  –Effect: Until the start of your next turn, treat all Battle Weathers as if they were
  1 Weather Tier lower. If this would reduce the Weather Tier to 0, ignore the effects
  of that Battle Weather. If you have 4+ Skill Ranks in Survival, you may treat it as 2
  Weather Tiers lower instead.

---

# The whole of what this does is a duration, so the whole of the script is putting one on
# and setting its clock. What being Braced is worth is in the mark's own file, which is
# where a reader looks for it.
[on used]
gain(braced);
expires(braced, start-of-next-turn);

# --- The clock ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Until the START of your next turn", which is a different edge from the one most of these
# use and the system already knows the difference: a start edge is never ahead of you
# during your own turn, so it is always the next one whichever turn you are standing in.
# Brace on your turn and it lifts when your next turn begins; nothing about it can be made
# to last two turns by using it out of sequence.
#
# --- What is not built, and why ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# Battle Weathers. This system has none - no Weather list, no Weather Tiers, nothing that
# reads one - so the reduction is said rather than applied: `weather.tiers` carries what
# you are entitled to, the sheet says what it comes to, and the table takes it off whatever
# Weather is in play. When Battle Weathers land there is one number to read and one place
# to read it from.
#
# "Minions: Free." There are no Minions in this system, which the Arrogant Declaration,
# Analysis and Hype files all say about their own Minion lines. Carried as printed.
#
# --- How it is gained --------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A Special Maneuver, so nobody has it until an effect hands it over. No Skill opens it
# yet, so the sheet says "gained through an effect" rather than naming one.
#
# Survival is the obvious candidate - it is the Skill this entry already reads, and the
# rule is "each Skill either provides an Adventuring Maneuver and/or a Special Maneuver for
# gaining 2+ Skill Ranks in that Skill". It is not built on a guess: the Survival entry
# will say, and connecting it is one line in the Skill table beside Investigation's and
# Performance's.
#
# Worth noticing when that line is written: this entry reads Survival Ranks twice at two
# different numbers. 2+ would be what opens the Maneuver and 4+ is what doubles it, and
# neither is the other.
